          "literatureReview": "Oral Glucose Tolerance Test (OGTT) evaluates glucose homeostasis. Procedure: 75g glucose load after overnight fast. Normal: fasting <100 mg/dL, 2hr <140 mg/dL. Impaired fasting glucose: 100-125 mg/dL. Impaired glucose tolerance: 2hr 140-199 mg/dL. Diabetes: fasting ≥126 mg/dL or 2hr ≥200 mg/dL. Extended test provides detailed glucose curve. Contraindications: uncontrolled diabetes, recent MI, pregnancy complications. Used for gestational diabetes screening and diabetes diagnosis when HbA1c inconclusive. Critical for comprehensive glucose metabolism assessment."
